# the printer settings Alt-Help's dump follows (Setprt): XControl 1.0
# (Atari, freeware) and its Printer CPX change them, then Alt-Help. Drive A is
# an .ST copy of XControl's disk (XCONTROL.ACC at its root) with its
# CPX\PRINTER.CPX also at the root, where XControl looks (A:\*.CPX;
# disk_copy.py --copy). Low resolution, TOS 1.x desktop positions.
@printer
@disk-a tools/dev/builds/disks/xcontrol.st
wait 100
key 0x01
desktop 2500
wait 50
# the first click after boot is lost: an empty spot first
mouse 280 180
click left 2
wait 25
# Desk > Control Panel (XControl)
mouse 24 5
wait 25
mouse 84 31
click left 2
wait 200
shot panel
# open Printer Setup (a double click: 60 ms between its events opens it on
# TOS 2.06 too, where 100 ms is too slow)
mouse 182 82
wait 25
dblclick 60
wait 150
shot printcpx
# Quality: Draft -> Final
mouse 162 144
click left 2
wait 50
mouse 170 165
click left 2
wait 50
shot final
# OK (the settings take effect: Setprt), then close XControl's window
mouse 159 180
click left 2
wait 100
mouse 36 17
click left 2
wait 100
# Alt-Help: the screen dump, with the new settings
printwatch
keydown 0x38
key 0x62
keyup 0x38
# Final quality doubles the dump (127,500 bytes; Draft 64,026): at least
# 120,000 bytes shows the setting took
printer 120000 9000
shot after
